```

`g_string_append_uri_escaped(str, host, IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS, TRUE)` calls `_uri_encoder(str, host, strlen(host), IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS, TRUE)`.

In `_uri_encoder`, processing `::1%\xC3`:
- `p` = `::1%\xC3`. `*p = ':'`. `is_valid(':', IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS)`? Let me check. `IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS` includes `:`. So `is_valid` returns TRUE. Append `:`. `p++`.
- ... processes `::1%` ...
- `p` = `\xC3` (last byte). `*p = 0xC3 >= 0x80`. `end - p = 1`. `g_utf8_get_char_validated(p, 1)` returns -2 (partial). So the condition is FALSE. Goes to else branch. `is_valid(0xC3, IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS)`? `g_uri_char_is_unreserved(0xC3)` = FALSE. `strchr(IP_ADDR_ALLOWED_CHARS, 0xC3)` = NULL. So `is_valid` returns FALSE. So it escapes: append `%`, `hex[0xC3 >> 4]` = `hex[0xC]` = `'C'`, `hex[0xC3 & 0xf]` = `hex[3]` = `'3'`. `p++`. Loop ends.

